# No Dev / Start Servers

The agent must **never** start the application or a long-running server to validate work.

## Forbidden

Do not run any of the following (including via yarn/npm/pnpm, or equivalent):

- `dev` / `next dev` / `yarn dev` / `npm run dev`
- `start` / `next start` / `yarn start` / `npm start`
- `test:watch` / `vitest` without `run` (watch mode)
- Any other long-running process meant to serve or hot-reload the app

Do not ask the user to start `dev`/`start` as a substitute for agent validation.

## Allowed validation

Use only static/CI-style checks:

- Typecheck: `yarn tsc --noEmit` (or project typecheck script if added)
- Lint: `yarn lint`
- Tests: `yarn test` (`vitest run` only — no watch)

Prefer these over building/serving when checking correctness. `yarn build` is allowed only when specifically needed to verify a production build failure, not as a default check.
